published: unknown\n</document_metadata>\n\nTechnical Proposal\nCase Management & Referral Tracking Platform for the Ministry of Social Development\nSubmitted in response to MSD/IT/2023-009\nExecutive Summary\nWe are pleased to submit this proposal for the design, development, and deployment of a unified case\nmanagement and referral tracking platform for the Ministry of Social Development (MSD), replacing a\nfragmented set of spreadsheet-based tools used across 9 regional offices. Our team combines deep\npublic-sector delivery experience with proven expertise in secure, offline-capable field data systems.\nUnderstanding of the Requirements\nMSD required a web-based case management system with a companion mobile app for field caseworkers,\nintegration with the national social registry API, migration of over 40,000 existing case records, and a\n12-month post-launch support period.\nProposed Approach & Methodology\nWe proposed a phased Agile delivery across four stages: discovery and requirements validation,\narchitecture and data model design, iterative development with bi-weekly stakeholder demos, and a\nstructured UAT and training rollout across all 9 regional offices.\nOutcome\nThe project was delivered on schedule over 8 months, followed by a 12-month support engagement. The\nplatform has processed over 60,000 case records since go-live, with a reported 35% reduction in average\ncase processing time across regional offices."}}]]